.TH SDSS 1
.SH NAME
sdss \- Steam / Discord status scheduler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sdss
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sdss
runs a user-session daemon that applies Discord and Steam presence from a work schedule,
with D-Bus controls and optional GTK settings and tray icon.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR sdss " / " sdss run
Start the scheduler. With no GUI features, use
.BR "sdss run --headless" .
.TP
.B sdss doctor
Print live status from the running daemon, or a local config summary.
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.TP
.B sdss migrate
Import legacy Python configuration into TOML and keyring.
.RB [ \-\-dry-run ]
.TP
.B sdss validate
Parse and validate
.IR ~/.config/sdss/config.toml .
.TP
.B sdss holidays list
List cached holiday bundles (year range and source).
.TP
.BI "sdss holidays refresh" " [ CC ]"
Download or refresh holiday data from Nager.Date (default: config country).
.TP
.BI "sdss override set" " MODE " "[ \-\-ttl SECONDS ]"
Request a temporary presence override via D-Bus (\fBinvisible\fR or \fBonline\fR).
Default TTL is 0 (until the next schedule change, at most 8 hours). Use an explicit duration for a fixed TTL.
.TP
.B sdss override clear
Clear override via D-Bus.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SDSS_DISCORD_API_URL
Override the Discord REST base URL (testing / mocking).
.TP
.B SDSS_NAGER_API_BASE
Override the Nager.Date API base URL (default
.BR https://date.nager.at ).
.TP
.B SDSS_REGENERATE_HOLIDAYS
If set to
.B 1
or
.BR true ,
the build script may run
.I tools/export-holidays/export.py
for dev-only JSON fixtures (not used at runtime).
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Tracing filter for stderr (default when not logging to the journal).
.TP
.B JOURNAL_STREAM / INVOCATION_ID
When built with the
.B journald
feature, these systemd variables select journald logging instead of plain stderr format.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sdss/config.toml
Main configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/sdss/state.json
Override and apply bookkeeping.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/sdss/discord_token.secret
Optional token file fallback if the keyring cannot be used.
.SH SEE ALSO
User unit:
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/sdss.service
(if installed).
